SteamARM: track self-modifying code in 16 KiB blocks (STEAMARM_FEX_SMC_BLOCK overrides).
The runtime backs 4 KiB guest pages with 16 KiB host pages carrying the union of their
protections, so a translated guest page stays write-protected only while every guest page
of its host page is: FEX now protects, invalidates and unprotects whole blocks, and drops
the protection of a block's other pages when one becomes writable. Minecraft Dungeons II's
protector rewrites stubs in a 16 MiB ring; stores into pages sharing a host page with a
writable one went unseen and it ran stale translations (benchmarks/stage62, 15 q).

